---
import DocsLayout from '../../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Ingest Footage — MHA Manager"
  description="Bring raw capture footage into your project as Capture Data assets and queue it — manually or automatically."
  currentSlug="ingest"
>

  <div class="doc-header">
    <h1 class="doc-title">Ingest Footage</h1>
    <p class="doc-lead">
      Every job runs on a <code>UFootageCaptureData</code> asset. Ingest turns raw capture footage on
      disk into that asset and queues a job for it in one step — by hand for a single take, or
      automatically as takes arrive from a capture tool.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout-note">
    <strong>Requires Capture Manager.</strong> Ingest uses the engine's <code>CaptureManager</code>
    plugin (UE 5.7+, included with the engine). When it is unavailable the Ingest controls hide
    themselves — you can still create Capture Data through Epic's own MetaHuman Animator workflow and
    add it to the queue manually.
  </div>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Ingest a take folder</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      In the MHA Manager panel, the Ingest section's <strong>Ingest Folder...</strong> button takes a
      raw take folder of image sequences on disk. It scans the folder, creates the media assets
      (<code>UImgMediaSource</code> and, if present, audio), assembles them into a
      <code>UFootageCaptureData</code> asset, and queues a job — auto-detecting mono, stereo, or
      depth from what it finds in the folder.
    </p>
    <figure class="doc-figure">
      <div class="doc-img-placeholder">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="placeholder-icon"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><line x1="20" y1="4" x2="20" y2="4.01"/></svg>
        <span class="placeholder-name">ingest-folder-button.webp</span>
        <span class="placeholder-hint">MHA Manager panel Ingest section — "Ingest Folder..." button, with a queued job row appearing after ingest</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>The Ingest Folder button — pick a take folder, get a Capture Data asset and a queued job</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Ingest video files</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Folder ingest understands image-sequence takes only. For <code>.mov</code> / <code>.mp4</code>
      sources, use the video-ingest path on UE 5.8, exposed through the
      <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/mcp-toolset">MCP toolset</a>'s <code>ingest_video</code>
      tool. It extracts frames and builds the same Capture Data asset. Supply a second video for a
      stereo (HMC) pair, or leave it empty for a mono take; pass an optional audio file, and an
      <code>ffmpeg</code> path to enable the third-party encoder for clips the built-in decoder
      rejects.
    </p>
    <div class="callout callout-note">
      Give each take its own import directory under one actor folder (for example
      <code>/Game/.../Imports/&lt;Actor&gt;/&lt;Take&gt;</code>). The ingest refuses to write into a
      folder that already holds assets, and keeping takes under a shared actor folder is what lets
      calibration and identity discovery find each other for stereo shoots.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Auto-queue on ingest</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      For a hands-off pipeline, the <strong>Ingest</strong> section of
      <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/global-settings">Global Settings</a> can watch the
      project and queue takes as they appear — for example takes pushed from Live Link Hub or Capture
      Manager straight into the Content Browser:
    </p>
    <div class="field-list">
      <div class="opt-row header">
        <span>Setting</span>
        <span>What it does</span>
      </div>
      <div class="opt-row">
        <span><strong>Auto-Queue Ingested Takes</strong></span>
        <span>Watches the project for newly created Footage Capture Data assets and adds each to the queue automatically. Takes already in the queue are not re-added.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="opt-row">
        <span><strong>Auto-Start Batch on Ingest</strong></span>
        <span>Starts the batch when auto-queued takes arrive and no batch is running. Takes arriving mid-batch are queued and started on the next idle trigger.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="opt-row">
        <span><strong>Watch Folder (optional)</strong></span>
        <span>A content-path prefix to limit the watch, e.g. <code>/Game/CaptureManager/Ingest</code>. Empty watches everywhere under <code>/Game</code>.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">What happens to an ingested take</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      However a take enters the queue, it is classified automatically and readied to process:
    </p>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Its <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/job-types">job type</a> is derived from the take — path-name tokens drive <code>grid</code>/<code>calib</code> -&gt; Stereo Calibration and <code>identity</code>/<code>dna</code> -&gt; Identity Create, while mono / stereo / audio come from the asset itself.</li>
      <li>Mono takes get a first-frame framing probe that auto-enables body tracking when the whole body is in shot.</li>
      <li>Dependent assets (calibration, identity) are auto-discovered where the folder layout allows, so a stereo take lands ready or clearly marked for what it still needs.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="callout callout-tip">
      Keep <code>grid</code>, <code>calib</code>, <code>identity</code>, and <code>dna</code> out of
      folder and take names that are <em>not</em> those take types — those tokens drive
      classification, and a misnamed performance take will be queued as the wrong job.
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="doc-footer">
    <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/quick-start" class="prev-link">
      <span class="nav-label">Previous</span>
      <span class="nav-title">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M19 12H5M12 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg>
        Quick Start
      </span>
    </a>
    <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/mono-workflow" class="next-link">
      <span class="nav-label">Next</span>
      <span class="nav-title">
        Mono Workflow
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .doc-header { margin-bottom: 32px; }

  .doc-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .doc-lead {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 620px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .doc-lead code,
  .section-desc code,
  .opt-row code,
  .bullet-list code,
  .callout code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .doc-section { margin-bottom: 44px; }

  .section-title {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section-desc {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .section-desc strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .bullet-list {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .bullet-list li {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-left: 4px;
  }

  .bullet-list li strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .field-list {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .opt-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2.4fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 11px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    align-items: start;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .opt-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .opt-row.header {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .opt-row strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .callout {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }

  .callout code { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg-surface) 60%, transparent); }
  .callout strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .callout em { color: var(--text); font-style: italic; }

  .callout-note {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent);
  }

  .callout-tip {
    border-left: 3px solid #f0a500;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #f0a500 8%, transparent);
  }

  .doc-figure { margin: 8px 0 0; }

  .doc-img-placeholder {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 32px 20px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .placeholder-icon { opacity: 0.5; }
  .placeholder-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .placeholder-hint { font-size: 0.775rem; max-width: 420px; line-height: 1.5; }

  .doc-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .doc-footer {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .prev-link, .next-link {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
    min-width: 140px;
  }

  .prev-link { align-items: flex-start; }
  .next-link { align-items: flex-end; }
  .prev-link:hover, .next-link:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }

  .nav-label { font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--text-muted); }

  .nav-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .opt-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
